<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- VANILLA_BEAST_EXCISION_1 wave 3: the caravan pack-carrier route.

     Engine rule (decompiled 1.6, PawnGroupKindWorker_Trader): a trader group can visit a home map only if one
     of its carriers' races is in that map biome's allowedPackAnimals, and the carrier is drawn from that same
     intersection. So the carrier a player sees = faction carriers ∩ biome allowedPackAnimals.

     1. Every trader group gains the OWNED pack beasts our biomes already allow (the union of the non-official
        allowedPackAnimals across our BiomeDefs, measured by vanilla_beast_carriers.py, not chosen here). Which
        one shows up where stays decided by each biome's own allowedPackAnimals. This alone opens trade
        caravans into RM_LongShade, RM_Stillsand, RUT_Desert and RUT_ExtremeDesert, whose allowed lists named
        only owned beasts that no faction carried, so no caravan could generate there at all.
        [not(RSW_Bantha)] keeps it idempotent against the two Utinni patches that ADD whole trader groups
        (DeepDesertTribes.xml, HomesteadDefenseLeague.xml): patch files load in directory order, so those groups
        carry the same lines literally and this op skips them if it happens to run second. So does
        RUT_Jawa_FreeDroidEnclaves' own FactionDef (it had no carriers node at all, so it never generated).
        PACK_ANIMALS_RESTORE_EMPTY_SADDLES added Kybuck, Skalder, Dewback and Fambaa: the owned pack beasts that
        PackAnimals_RestoreSaddles.xml now allows. The owned RM_ carriers (RM_Tirbak, RM_Vellak, RM_Vaalok) are NOT
        here: the free tier gives every trader group them (RimMandrake WeepingStones/Stillsand
        Patches/RM_TraderCarriers_*.xml, card 2026-10-11), and that mod loads before this one.
     2. RM_LanternDeeps keeps Muffalo and Alpaca: they are its only pack animals since its beetles were cut
        (66a0d9db1), so removing them would close the Deeps to every caravan. An owned carrier is its sitting's work.

     Proof: python3 src/RimMandrake/Utils/vanilla_beast_carriers.py with the simulate flag on this file (exit 0 = no faction loses
     a biome it could trade into, and no official carrier is left in a touched biome). The simulator models
     exactly these two op shapes and refuses any other, so keep new ops to them. -->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Trader"]/carriers[not(RSW_Bantha)]</xpath>
    <value>
      <RSW_Bantha MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Bantha>
      <RSW_Ronto MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Ronto>
      <RSW_Eopie MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Eopie>
      <RSW_Jamel MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Jamel>
      <RSW_Falumpaset MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Falumpaset>
      <RSW_Kybuck MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Kybuck>
      <RSW_Skalder MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Skalder>
      <RSW_Dewback MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Dewback>
      <RSW_Fambaa MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">2</RSW_Fambaa>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
